🚀 Features

✅ User Registration with unique username & email
✅ User Login with username/email + password
✅ Profile Dashboard displaying user details
✅ Responsive UI with modern animations
✅ SQLite Database integration for persistence
✅ Simple logout mechanism

🛠 Tech Stack

Frontend: HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript

Backend: Node.js, Express.js

Database: SQLite3

Middleware: Body-Parser

📂 Project Structure
project-root/
│── public/
│   └── index.html     # Frontend UI
│── server.js          # Backend API (Express + SQLite)
│── users.db           # SQLite database (auto-created)
│── package.json       # Node.js dependencies

⚙️ Installation
1. Clone the Repository
git clone https://github.com/your-username/hygienic-food-app.git
cd hygienic-food-app

2. Install Dependencies
npm install express sqlite3 body-parser

3. Start the Server
node server.js


Server will run at:
👉 http://localhost:5000

💻 Usage

Open the app in your browser: http://localhost:5000

Create a new account using Register

Log in using your credentials

Access your profile information

Logout anytime

🗄 Database

The app uses SQLite (users.db) with the following schema:

Column	Type	Constraints
id	INTEGER	Primary Key (Auto Increment)
name	TEXT	Not Null
email	TEXT	Unique, Not Null
username	TEXT	Unique, Not Null
password	TEXT	Not Null

⚠️ Note: Passwords are currently stored in plain text (only for demo purposes).

🔒 Security Considerations

Passwords are not hashed → Use bcrypt or similar in production

No authentication tokens/sessions → Add JWT or session middleware for real-world use

Database should have proper validation & sanitation for inputs

